WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
A BCH wallet can change. A Nostr identity can persist. Which wallet is authorized now?

2
00:12.000 --> 00:30.000
KYVERA binds two independent keys: BCH and Nostr. Both signatures are verified locally.

3
00:30.000 --> 00:50.000
Signed records form a hash-linked authorization chain. Relays only supply evidence.

4
00:50.000 --> 00:70.000
An authorized rotation moves the current wallet to B and marks A superseded.

5
00:70.000 --> 00:82.000
Wallet A's historical proof stays valid. It is simply no longer current.

6
00:82.000 --> 00:90.000
KYVERA. Keys change. Trust shouldn't disappear.
